From 71785b89f625015539b1e5a78b57dae8dbbb3dda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:57:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/40] fix(format): readable number printing (FC-01), escaped
 CLI diagnostics (FC-06)

FC-01: render wrote exponents below -1000 (e.g. 1.0e-1000 -> 10e-1001)
that parse rejects, so fmt output of a check-passing document could not be
read back. Scientific notation is now used only while |e| <= maxExponent,
positional notation otherwise.

FC-06: figram check/fmt and figram-engine printed names from the document
raw (ESC sequences, LF forging an 'ok' line, NUL). New Format.sanitize
escapes C0, DEL and C1 as \u00XX in all CLI diagnostics.

Verified on a stage0 (4.35.0, 5f4537b2) build only; bin/ not regenerated.

(cherry picked from commit 4a38b911652c3e5e85eb87a54d2f7a1f89f944c0)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JgWRtX2jyUidN8gxEhe5qx
